WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.660
In a devastating bit of news, it was revealed&nbsp;
on November 20, 2022, that Supernatural actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.200
Nicki Aycox died on November 16. Aycox's&nbsp;
sister-in-law, Susan Raab Ceklosky broke the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.060
news in a Facebook post that the 47-year-old&nbsp;
actor and musician had passed away, writing,

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:36.840
Aycox was diagnosed with leukemia in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.186 --> 00:00:40.306
but her cause of death has not&nbsp;
been revealed as of this video.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.620
Aycox is perhaps best known&nbsp;
for her role as Meg Masters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.400
the original host of the Meg&nbsp;
entity in The CW's Supernatural.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:51.934
"You killed those two people for nothing.&nbsp;
Baby, I've killed a lot more for a lot less."

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:56.220
She was a prolific actor who appeared in a&nbsp;
number of high-profile projects over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:01.492
including the psychological thriller Perfect&nbsp;
Stranger and the horror film Jeepers Creepers&nbsp;2. 

00:01:01.492 --> 00:01:05.930
She also had a role in the second X-Files&nbsp;
movie, The X-Files: I Want to Believe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.625
making her one of the few stars who have&nbsp;
appeared in both Supernatural and The X-Files.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:15.720
Nicki Aycox's talents as an actor were evident&nbsp;
to anyone who saw her performances on screens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.260
big and small. The people who worked&nbsp;
with her have also been quick to note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:23.048
that she was quite an exceptional&nbsp;
person as well behind the scenes.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:26.546
Supernatural boss Eric Kripke wrote on Twitter,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.100
"Lackluster men."

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.740
Supernatural regular Jim Beaver also shared&nbsp;
his memories of Aycox on Twitter, writing,

00:01:55.421 --> 00:02:00.480
Other people associated with Aycox's work, like&nbsp;
The X-Files: I Want to Believe screenwriter Frank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.510
Spotnitz and fellow Meg actor Rachel Miner,&nbsp;
have also posted their own condolences.

00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:11.400
Aycox retired from acting in 2014. The following&nbsp;
year, she released her first and only album,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.260
Red Velvet Room, which contains five&nbsp;
original songs created by Aycox herself.
 &nbsp;

00:02:16.706 --> 00:02:20.520
Thanks to her far-reaching work in the&nbsp;
entertainment world, Nicki Aycox has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:25.560
collaborated with a laundry list of well-known&nbsp;
creatives. In doing so, she's amassed a sprawling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.640
fanbase that wraps around the world, who've&nbsp;
come to appreciate the work she put in when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.960
the cameras were rolling. With the news of her&nbsp;
death at the forefront of the media, fans came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.720
out in droves to honor Aycox's legacy in the form&nbsp;
of heartfelt social media posts. One fan Tweeted,

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:52.920
"I'm Meg."

00:02:53.444 --> 00:02:54.420
Someone else tweeted,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.820
Yet another fan noted how especially devastating&nbsp;
Aycox's passing is due to its close proximity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.260
to those of fellow pop culture icons&nbsp;
Kevin Conroy and Jason David Frank.

00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:15.960
This is just the tip of the iceberg when it comes&nbsp;
to online tributes dedicated to Aycox. Evidently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.140
she left a lasting impact on&nbsp;
folks from all walks of life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.760
